<title>USA: Interpublic takes stake in Nicholson - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Interpublic takes stake in Nicholson - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Advertising agency holding company Interpublic Group of Cos Inc is expected to announce today it took a minority stake in Nicholson New York, a firm which helps companies determine what to do on the Web, the Wall Street Journal said in Thursday's electronic edition.</p>
<p>Terms would not be disclosed, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Nicholson's clients included IBM, Sony Corp, Reader's Digest Association and Harper Collins, the Journal said.</p>
